      "title": "The Garden by the Field",
      "text": "Last spring, a group of students at Brookdale High noticed an empty plot beside the sports field. The ground was covered with weeds and broken bottles, but the students saw a possible garden. They asked the town council for permission and collected old wooden boxes from local shops. With help from a science teacher, they built raised beds and filled them with soil donated by a nearby farm.\n\nEach Saturday, volunteers water the plants and record how quickly they grow. Younger children from the neighbourhood visit after school to learn about herbs and insects. In July, the students picked their first tomatoes and gave baskets to a small community kitchen. They also kept some vegetables for a lunch stand during school events.\n\nThe garden has not solved every problem in the area, yet it has made the field feel safer and more welcoming. “People used to walk past quickly,” says student leader Nia Patel. “Now they stop and talk.” The students hope the garden will show that young people can improve shared spaces through patient work.",
      "table": null
    },
